<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Plan of Iguala</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1821</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Plan of the Three Guarantees</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Plan of Iguala was the programme for Mexican independence proclaimed on 24 February 1821 at Iguala by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agustin-de-iturbide">Agustín de Iturbide</a> and agreed with the insurgent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vicente-guerrero">Vicente Guerrero</a>. It promised three guarantees: independence under a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitutional-monarchy">constitutional monarchy</a>, the Catholic religion, and the union and equality of Spaniards and Mexicans. Its Army of the Three Guarantees won rapid support and entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a> in September 1821.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/plan-of-iguala.jpg" alt="Plan of Iguala" width="320" height="460" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: rm porrua · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plan_de_Iguala_foja_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
